cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Arithmetic landscapes: manuscripts, Lean development and verification apparatus"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amauchi
    given-names: Kentaro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0890-4395"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mathlab0911/arithmetic-landscapes"
url: "https://mathlab0911.github.io/"
abstract: >-
  A research repository in number theory. Three manuscripts study the subset-sum landscape of a
  finite set of odd integers: the ratio of strict local minima to ground states converges to a
  rational invariant read off the set by counting, and that invariant is the annealed
  (independence) prediction itself, so the main theorem says the annealed count of metastable
  states is asymptotically exact. A lower bound that would normally cost a quantitative
  equidistribution estimate is obtained instead from the Kubert distribution relation as an
  exact equality. The repository contains the manuscripts, a Lean 4 development of the settled
  results with an independent kernel-replay checker, the scripts and logs behind every number
  quoted in the text, and a full record of the mistakes the process has made. The manuscripts
  are not peer-reviewed; every theorem, proposition and lemma declares its status where it is
  stated.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - additive combinatorics
  - subset sum
  - local minima
  - Kubert distribution relation
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - disordered systems
